> If I do the configuration by hand in /etc/modules.conf, I get an error 
> saying that 'parm_snd_pcm_channels_p' and 'parm_snd_pcm_channels_c' do 
> not exist (sorry, I don't have the exact output to hand)
 
these module parameters are obsolete on 0.9.0 (they are for 0.5.x
drivers).  sorry if you referred to INSTALL in alsa-driver.  the
document was wrong.  now it's fixed.


> If someone could mail me the correct values and a quick how-to on 
> getting the damn thing fired up, I'd much appreciate it.

please remove all module options from snd-es1968 (except for
snd_index).  it should work as default.

also, please make sure that the version of your alsa-utils / alsa-lib
is really 0.9.0.


